{"bio":[{"AwardsAndAccomplishments":" ","CareerHighlights":"SINGLES<br>\nWinner (3): 2026 - Wimbledon, Berlin<br>\n2024 - Monterrey<br>\n<br>\nFinalist (5): 2025 - Tokyo, Beijing, Prague<br>\n2023 - Prague, Adelaide #1<br>\n<br>\nDOUBLES<br>\nWinner (2): 2026 - Cincinnati (w/Bouzkova), Berlin (w/Alexandrova)<br>\n<br>\nFinalist (2): 2025 - Rouen (w/Khromacheva)<br>\n2024 - Abu Dhabi (w/Watson)<br>\n<br>","CareerHighlightsDoubles":" ","CareerHighlightsSingles":"Reached three Tour finals in 2025, including her first career WTA 1000 final at Beijing (l. Anisimova), as well as runner-up showings at Prague and Tokyo; made her Top 20 debut and finished at a career-high No.13 in the year-end rankings<br>\n<br>\nIn 2024, achieved first Grand Slam singles quarterfinal at the Australian Open (l. Yastremska), where she also defeated then-World No.1 Iga Swiatek in the 3r; won her first singles title at Monterrey (d. Sun in F); reached SF at Prague (l. eventual champion Linette) and Brisbane (l. eventual champion Rybakina); earned a new career-high ranking of No.25 on August 26, 2024<br>\n<br>\nBreakthrough year in 2023, achieving runner-up twice; Adelaide 1 (as qualifier, l. Sabalenka) and Prague (l. Hibino). Also reached quarterfinals at Lyon (l. Osorio) and 3r at Indian Wells (l. Gauff) and Cincinnati  (as qualifier, l. Gauff). Broke into Top 40 on October 9, 2023.<br>\n<br>\nMade Top 100 debut on August 1, 2022, following SF run at Prague (l. eventual champion Bouzkova); overtook Gauff at the youngest player in Top 100<br>\n<br>\nAlso reached 2r at Tallinn (as qualifier, l. Haddad Maia) and fell 1r at both Roland Garros (as qualifier, l. Raducanu) and US Open (as qualifier, l. Bouzkova). On ITF Circuit, lifted fifth and sixth titles at this level, winning W60 tournament in Croissy-Beaubourg, France and W100 event in Versmold, Germany<br>\n<br>\nFinished 2021 campaign with 38-9 win-loss record, winning four ITF Circuit titles, including at W60 event in Prerov, Czech Republic<br>\n<br>\nMade WTA qualifying debut at 2020 Prague<br>\n<br>\nOn ITF Circuit, owns six titles in singles and one in doubles<br>\n<br>\nAs a junior, won 2021 girls' singles at Roland Garros","CareerInReview":"2024 - Achieved first Grand Slam singles quarterfinal appearance at the Australian Open (l. Yastremska), where she also defeated then-World No.1 Iga Swiatek in the 3r; won her first singles title at Monterrey (d. Sun in F); reached SF at Prague (l. eventual champion Linette) and Brisbane (l. eventual champion Rybakina); earned a new career-high ranking of World No.25 on August 26, 2024<br>\n<br>\n2023 - Breakthrough year, achieving runner-up twice; Adelaide 1 (as qualifier, l. Sabalenka) and Prague (l. Hibino). Also reached quarterfinals at Lyon (l. Osorio) and 3r at Indian Wells (l. Gauff) and Cincinnati  (as qualifier, l. Gauff). Earned career-high ranking of No. 40 on October 9, 2023.<br>\n<br>\n2022 - Made Top-100 debut on August 1, 2022, following SF run at Prague (l. eventual champion Bouzkova) overtaking Gauff as the youngest player in Top 100. Reached 2r at Tallinn (as qualifier, l. Haddad Maia) and fell 1r at both Roland Garros (as qualifier, l. Raducanu) and US Open (as qualifier, l. Bouzkova).<br>\n<br>\n2021 - As a junior, won 2021 girls' singles at Roland Garros and won four ITF circuit titles, including W60 event at Prerov, Czech Republic<br>\n<br> \n2020 - Made WTA qualifying debut at Prague<br>\n<br>","CurrentYearDetail":"Made QF at US Open (l. Sabalenka)<br>\n<br>\nReached R16 at Cincinnati (l. Anisimova)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 2r at Toronto (1r bye, l. McNally)<br>\n<br>\nWon maiden Grand Slam title at Wimbledon (d. Muchova in F)<br>\n<br>\nFell 1r at Bad Homburg (l. Ruse)<br>\n<br>\nWon second career WTA title at Berlin (d. Pegula in F)<br>\n<br>\nFell 1r at Roland Garros (l. Sakkari)<br>\n<br>\nReached 4r at Rome (l. Cirstea)<br>\n<br>\nMade QF at Madrid (l. Kostyuk)<br>\n<br>\nReached QF at Stuttgart (l. Svitolina)<br>\n<br>\nMade 2r at Miami (l. Cirstea)<br>\n<br>\nReached SF at Indian Wells (l. eventual champion Sabalenka)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 2r at Dubai (l. Cirstea)<br>\n<br>\nMade 2r at Doha (l. Gracheva)<br>\n<br>\nReached 3r at Australian Open (l. X.Wang)<br>\n<br>\nOpened season at Brisbane reaching 2r (l. M.Andreeva)","activeFlag":"A","additional":" ","age":21,"apparel":null,"apparellink":null,"backhand":"N/A","birthcity":"Vsetin, Czech Republic","careerprize":12051608,"countryname":"Czechia","datebioupdated":"2026-09-28T00:00:00+00:00","dateofbirth":"2004-11-17T00:00:00+00:00","dblcareerlost":72,"dblcareertitles":2,"dblcareerwon":72,"dblhirank":36,"dblhirankdate":"2026-08-24T00:00:00+00:00","dblrank":37,"dblytdlost":12,"dblytdtitles":2,"dblytdwon":13,"facebook":"","firstname":"Linda","height":"5' 10'' (1.79m)","imagecredit":"","imageurl":"https://wtafiles.blob.core.windows.net/images/headshots/329668.jpg","lastname":"Noskova","natlcode":"CZE","personal":"Currently coached by Tomas Krupa<br>\nMother's name is Ivana Noskova; Father's name is Drahos Nosek<br>\nLike listening to Maneskin, Lil Nas X, Lizzo<br>\nEnjoys watching Wrestling and streaming Netflix<br>\nAlso likes to swim, run, and spend time with pets<br>\nFavorite player is Serena Williams","photocredit":null,"playerid":329668,"playhand":"Right-Handed","pronunciation":"","proyear":null,"racquet":null,"racquetlink":null,"residence":"Prerov, Czech Republic","sglcareerlost":113,"sglcareertitles":3,"sglcareerwon":217,"sglhirank":6,"sglhirankdate":"2026-08-24T00:00:00+00:00","sglrank":6,"sglytdlost":14,"sglytdtitles":2,"sglytdwon":33,"shoes":null,"shoeslink":null,"status":"Pro","twitter":"","website":"","ytdprize":7490989},{"AwardsAndAccomplishments":" ","CareerHighlights":"SINGLES<br>\nWinner (5): 2025 - Linz<br>\n2023 -'s-Hertogenbosch<br> \n2022 - 's-Hertogenbosch, Seoul<br>\n2020 - Shenzhen<br>\n<br>\nFinalist (8): 2026 - Abu Dhabi<br>\n2025 - Ningbo, Seoul, Monterrey<br> \n2024 - Linz<br> \n2023 - Cleveland<br>\n2021 - Moscow<br>\n2018 - Linz<br>\n<br>\nDOUBLES<br>\nWinner (3): 2026 - Berlin (w/Noskova), Abu Dhabi (w/Joint)<br>\n2019 - Budapest (w/Zvonareva)<br>\n<br>\nFinalist (1): 2025 - Stuttgart (w/Zhang)<br>\n<br>\nWTA 125 TITLES AND FINALS<br>\nSINGLES<br> \nWinner (3): 2019 - Limoges<br>\n2018 - Limoges<br>\n2016 - Limoges<br>\n<br>","CareerHighlightsDoubles":" ","CareerHighlightsSingles":"In 2025 claimed first career WTA 500 title at Linz and reached three additional finals all at 500 events; Monterrey, Seoul and Ningbo. Made her Top 10 debut on October 13 and finished the season inside the Top 10<br>\n<br>\nPlayed WTA Finals debut match at the 2025 WTA Finals as an alternate in the round robin stage, lost to eventual champion Elena Rybakina<br>\n<br>\nIn 2024, highlights included reaching the final at Linz (l. Ostapenko in Final) and semifinals at Adelaide (l. eventual champion Ostapenko), Miami (l. eventual champion Collins), 's-Hertogenbosch (l. eventual champion Samsonova) and Monterrey (l. Sun); also made quarterfinals at Wuhan (l. Xin. Wang) and her best Grand Slam result of the season came during a 3r run at US Open (l. eventual champion Sabalenka)<br>\n<br>\nIn 2023, won fourth career singles title at 's-Hertogenbosch, successfully defending the title and defeating top seed, Kudermetova in the final. A run of successful results followed with SF at Berlin (l. eventual champion, Kvitova), 4r at Wimbledon (l. Sabalenka) - a career best result at any of the majors and runner-up at Cleveland (l. Sorribes Tormo).<br>\n<br>\nReached a 2023 peak ranking of No. 16 on February 20 following a 3r finish at Australian Open (l. Linette), before posting two QF results at Miami (l. eventual champion Kvitova) and Charleston (l. Bencic). Another QF then came in the Asian Swing at Tokyo (l. Pavlyuchenkova).<br>\n<br>\nIn 2022, won titles at ‘s-Hertogenbosch (d. Sabalenka in F) and Seoul (d. Ostapenko in F). Also advanced to SF at Charleston, Madrid and Ostrava, making Top 20 debut on October 10, 2022<br>\n<br>\nReached third WTA singles final in 2021, enjoying run to final at home tournament of Moscow (l. Kontaveit). Other key result was SF run at Gippsland Trophy (l. Kanepi)<br>\n<br>\nPosted two best wins-by-ranking of career in 2021, defeating No.2 Halep (Gippsland Trophy) and No.2 Sabalenka (Moscow)<br>\n<br>\nReached 2r on Olympic debut at Tokyo 2020<br>\n<br>\nOpened 2020 season by lifting her maiden WTA singles title, at Shenzhen (d. Rybakina in F)<br>\n<br>\nMade Top 50 debut on June 17, 2019 after QF run at 's-Hertogenbosch<br>\n<br>\nRegistered 30 Tour-level match wins during 2019, in which she reached SF at Budapest, Seoul and Linz and made QF at St. Petersburg, 's-Hertogenbosch, Eastbourne and Moscow. Also advanced to 3r at a major for the first time, at Roland Garros<br>\n<br>\nWon sole WTA doubles title at 2019 Budapest (w/Zvonareva)<br>\n<br>\nCame through qualifying to make maiden WTA final appearance at 2018 Linz (l. Giorgi)<br>\n<br>\nAdvanced to first WTA QF at 2018 Seoul, scoring maiden Top 10 win of her career en route, over No.10 Ostapenko<br>\n<br>\nMade Top 100 debut at No.93 on March 20, 2017 after winning title at $60K ITF/Shenzhen-CHN<br>\n<br>\nAt 2016 Wimbledon, ranked No.223, won her way through qualifying on her maiden Slam appearance, going on to reach 2r (upset No.23 seed Ivanovic in 1r)<br>\n<br>\nWon WTA 125K Series title at Limoges in 2016, 2018-19<br>\n<br>\nReached 2r on WTA main draw debut at 2016 Katowice (as qualifier, l. eventual R-Up Giorgi)<br>\n<br>\nContested qualifying for the first time at a WTA-level tournament at 2014 Bad Gastein<br>\n<br>\nPlayed first professional events of career on ITF Circuit in Europe in 2011<br>","CareerInReview":"2024 - Did not win a title but reached the final at Linz (l. Ostapenko in Final); she reached semifinals at Adelaide (l. eventual champion Ostapenko), Miami (l. eventual champion Collins), 's-Hertogenbosch (l. eventual champion Samsonova), and Monterrey (l. Sun). She also made the quarterfinals at Wuhan (l. Xin. Wang) and best grand slam result of the season came during a 3r run at US Open (l. eventual champion Sabalenka)<br>\n<br>\n2023 – Earned fourth career singles title at 's-Hertogenbosch, successfully defending the title and defeating top seed, Kudermetova in the final. A run of successful results followed with SF at Berlin (l. eventual champion, Kvitova), 4r at Wimbledon (l. Sabalenka) - a career best result at any of the majors and runner-up at Cleveland (l. Sorribes Tormo); reached career high ranking of 16 on February 20, 2023<br>\n<br>\n2022 - Won titles at ‘s-Hertogenbosch (d. Sabalenka in F) and Seoul (d. Ostapenko in F). Also advanced to SF at Charleston, Madrid and Ostrava, making Top-20 debut on October 10, 2022<br>\n<br>\n2021 - Finished year ranked No.33 (3rd consecutive Top 40 finish); reached third WTA singles final at home tournament of Moscow (R-Up, l. Kontaveit); other key result was SF run at Gippsland Trophy (l. Kanepi); posted two best wins-by-ranking of career defeating No.2 Halep (2021 Gippsland Trophy) and No.2 Sabalenka (2021 Moscow); contested Olympics for the first time, reaching 2r at Tokyo 2020.<br>\n<br>\n2020 - Finished season ranked No.35; opened season by lifting her maiden WTA singles title, at Shenzhen (d. Rybakina in F); other highlights included SF at St. Petersburg and Linz.<br>\n<br>\n2019 - Posted 30 tour-level match wins during 2019 season, in which she reached SF at Budapest, Seoul and Linz and made QF at St.Petersburg, 's-Hertogenbosch, Eastbourne and Moscow. Made Top 50 debut after QF run at 's-Hertogenbosch (June 17, 2019). Other highlights in 2019 included upset of No.5 Halep en route to R16 at Beijing - the first win of her career over a Top 5 player - and 3r showing at Roland Garros.<br>\n<br>\n2018 - Second Top 100 season (finishing No.93); runner-up at Linz (l. to Giorgi); QF at Seoul (l. to S.Hsieh); reached 2r three times (incl. Australian Open); fell 1r eight times (incl. other three majors) and in qualifying four times; won one WTA 125K Series singles title.<br>\n<br>\n2017 - Broke into the Top 100 on March 20, finishing the year at No.73. Played in all four Grand Slam main draws for the first time in her career, reaching 2r at Roland Garros and US Open. Achieved the best win of her career in Paris, defeating No.38 Siniakova in 1r. Also won a pair of ITF finals, giving her seven such titles throughout her career.<br>\n<br>\n2016 - Reached 2r three times (incl. at Wimbledon and on WTA main draw debut at Katowice); fell in qualifying five times; won one WTA 125K Series singles title.<br>\n<br>\n2015 - Continued to play on ITF Circuit.<br>\n<br>\n2014 - Played first WTA qualifying at Bad Gastein; won one singles title on ITF Circuit.<br>\n<br>\n2013 - Won three singles titles on ITF Circuit.<br>\n<br>\n2012 - Continued to play on ITF Circuit.<br>\n<br>\n2011 - Played first events on ITF Circuit.","CurrentYearDetail":"Reached 3r at US Open (l. Kostyuk)<br>\n<br>\nContested 2r at Monterrey (after 1r bye, l. Tauson)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 3r at Cincinnati (l. Bejlek)<br>\n<br>\nReached QF at Toronto (l. Svitolina)<br>\n<br>\nFell in 1r at Memphis (l. eventual champion Liutova via ret.)<br>\n<br>\nReached 3r at Wimbledon (l. Jovic)<br>\n<br>\nReached QF at Bad Homburg (l. Osaka)<br>\n<br>\nMade 2r at Berlin (l. Sabalenka)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 1r at 's-Hertogenbosch (l. Udvardy)<br>\n<br>\nFell 1r at Roland Garros (l. Osorio)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 2r at Strasbourg (l. Li)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 2r at Stuttgart (l. Noskova) and Rome (l. Siegemund)<br>\n<br>\nMade 2r at Linz (l. Pliskova)<br>\n<br>\nReached 3r at Miami (l. Cristian)<br>\n<br>\nPlayed 2r at Indian Wells (l. Gibson)<br>\n<br>\nContested 2r at Doha (l. Ostapenko) and Dubai (l. Linette)<br>\n<br>\nFinished R-Up at Abu Dhabi (l. champion Bejlek in F)<br>\n<br>\nFell 1r at Adelaide (l. Cristian) and Australian Open (l. Sonmez)<br>\n<br>\nOpened season with 3r at Brisbane (l. Muchova)<br>","activeFlag":"A","additional":" ","age":31,"apparel":null,"apparellink":null,"backhand":"N/A","birthcity":"Chelyabinsk, Russia","careerprize":11264263,"countryname":"Russian Federation","datebioupdated":"2026-09-28T00:00:00+00:00","dateofbirth":"1994-11-15T00:00:00+00:00","dblcareerlost":106,"dblcareertitles":3,"dblcareerwon":84,"dblhirank":36,"dblhirankdate":"2026-03-02T00:00:00+00:00","dblrank":57,"dblytdlost":9,"dblytdtitles":2,"dblytdwon":14,"facebook":"","firstname":"Ekaterina","height":"5' 9'' (1.75m)","imagecredit":"","imageurl":"https://wtafiles.blob.core.windows.net/images/headshots/319007.jpg","lastname":"Alexandrova","natlcode":"RUS","personal":"Coached by Igor Andreev<br>\nWorked with her father, Evgeny. Was previously coached by Vojta Flegl<br>\nMother is Julia, also has sister, Anna, and brother Jury. Began playing tennis at age 6<br>\nFavorite shot is forehand; favorite surface is hard<br>\nSpeaks Russian, English and Czech<br>\nLikes to cook, especially making cakes<br>\nAdmires Serena Williams","photocredit":null,"playerid":319007,"playhand":"Right-Handed","pronunciation":"","proyear":null,"racquet":null,"racquetlink":null,"residence":"Prague, Czech Republic","sglcareerlost":310,"sglcareertitles":5,"sglcareerwon":483,"sglhirank":10,"sglhirankdate":"2025-10-13T00:00:00+00:00","sglrank":28,"sglytdlost":22,"sglytdtitles":0,"sglytdwon":17,"shoes":null,"shoeslink":null,"status":"Pro","twitter":"","website":"","ytdprize":1574260}],"headToHeadSummary":[{"isfinal":false,"losses":1,"opponentid":"319007","opponentnamefirst":"EKATERINA","opponentnamelast":"ALEXANDROVA","playerid":"329668","playernamefirst":"LINDA","playernamelast":"NOSKOVA","surface":"All","wins":1}],"matchEncounterResults":[{"Country":"FRANCE","DrawSizes":"64M/0Q/32D","PrizeMoney":null,"PrizeWon":0.0,"StartDate":"2024-07-27T00:00:00+00:00","Surface":"CLAY","TournamentLevel":null,"TournamentName":"OLYMPICS","TournamentType":"VS","city":"PARIS","entry_rank_1":null,"entry_rank_2":null,"entry_type_1":" ","entry_type_2":" ","player1Info":{"id":329668,"firstName":"Linda","lastName":"Noskova","fullName":"Linda Noskova","countryCode":"CZE","dateOfBirth":"2004-11-17","metadata":null},"player2Info":{"id":319007,"firstName":"Ekaterina","lastName":"Alexandrova","fullName":"Ekaterina Alexandrova","countryCode":"RUS","dateOfBirth":"1994-11-15","metadata":null},"player3Info":{"id":322191,"firstName":"Karolina","lastName":"Muchova","fullName":"Karolina Muchova","countryCode":"CZE","dateOfBirth":"1996-08-21","metadata":null},"player4Info":{"id":311220,"firstName":"Elena","lastName":"Vesnina","fullName":"Elena Vesnina","countryCode":"RUS","dateOfBirth":"1986-08-01","metadata":null},"player_1":"329668","player_2":"319007","player_3":"322191","player_4":"311220","points_1":0.0,"points_2":0.0,"points_bonus_1":null,"points_bonus_2":null,"points_champ_1":0.0,"points_champ_2":0.0,"qpm_flag":"M","rank_1":651,"rank_2":364,"rank_code_1":null,"rank_code_2":null,"reason_code":"W","round_name":"R32","s_d_flag":"D","scores":"2-6  7-6(5)  10-6","seed_1":null,"seed_2":null,"spc_rank_1":9,"spc_rank_2":303,"team_name_1":"MUCHOVA,  K.  CZE  /  NOSKOVA,  L.  CZE","team_name_2":"ALEXANDROVA,  E.  RUS  /  VESNINA,  E.  ","tourn_nbr":" 650","tourn_round":"1","tourn_year":"2024","winner":1},{"Country":"MEXICO","DrawSizes":"32M/16Q/16D","PrizeMoney":1064510.0,"PrizeWon":31100.0,"StartDate":"2025-08-18T00:00:00+00:00","Surface":"HARD","TournamentLevel":"P","TournamentName":"MONTERREY","TournamentType":"VS","city":"MONTERREY","entry_rank_1":null,"entry_rank_2":null,"entry_type_1":" ","entry_type_2":" ","player1Info":{"id":329668,"firstName":"Linda","lastName":"Noskova","fullName":"Linda Noskova","countryCode":"CZE","dateOfBirth":"2004-11-17","metadata":null},"player2Info":{"id":319007,"firstName":"Ekaterina","lastName":"Alexandrova","fullName":"Ekaterina Alexandrova","countryCode":"RUS","dateOfBirth":"1994-11-15","metadata":null},"player3Info":null,"player4Info":null,"player_1":"329668","player_2":"319007","player_3":"","player_4":"","points_1":108.0,"points_2":null,"points_bonus_1":null,"points_bonus_2":null,"points_champ_1":108.0,"points_champ_2":null,"qpm_flag":"M","rank_1":23,"rank_2":14,"rank_code_1":null,"rank_code_2":null,"reason_code":"W","round_name":"Q","s_d_flag":"S","scores":"7-6(5)  4-6  6-2","seed_1":6,"seed_2":2,"spc_rank_1":null,"spc_rank_2":null,"team_name_1":"NOSKOVA,  LINDA  CZE","team_name_2":"ALEXANDROVA,  EKATERINA  RUS","tourn_nbr":"1039","tourn_round":"3","tourn_year":"2025","winner":2},{"Country":"GERMANY","DrawSizes":"32M/16Q/16D","PrizeMoney":1206446.0,"PrizeWon":35000.0,"StartDate":"2026-04-13T00:00:00+00:00","Surface":"CLAY","TournamentLevel":"P","TournamentName":"STUTTGART","TournamentType":"VS","city":"STUTTGART","entry_rank_1":null,"entry_rank_2":null,"entry_type_1":" ","entry_type_2":" ","player1Info":{"id":329668,"firstName":"Linda","lastName":"Noskova","fullName":"Linda Noskova","countryCode":"CZE","dateOfBirth":"2004-11-17","metadata":null},"player2Info":{"id":319007,"firstName":"Ekaterina","lastName":"Alexandrova","fullName":"Ekaterina Alexandrova","countryCode":"RUS","dateOfBirth":"1994-11-15","metadata":null},"player3Info":null,"player4Info":null,"player_1":"329668","player_2":"319007","player_3":"","player_4":"","points_1":108.0,"points_2":1.0,"points_bonus_1":null,"points_bonus_2":null,"points_champ_1":108.0,"points_champ_2":1.0,"qpm_flag":"M","rank_1":14,"rank_2":13,"rank_code_1":null,"rank_code_2":null,"reason_code":"W","round_name":"R16","s_d_flag":"S","scores":"6-1  6-1","seed_1":null,"seed_2":8,"spc_rank_1":null,"spc_rank_2":null,"team_name_1":"ALEXANDROVA,  EKATERINA  RUS","team_name_2":"NOSKOVA,  LINDA  CZE","tourn_nbr":"1051","tourn_round":"2","tourn_year":"2026","winner":1}]}